+# Maintained Dobe Inspect transport
+
+This local integration is claimed by Codex on `codex/dobe-inspect`, against the
+owner's complete Dobe Local/Cloud plan. It does not claim an upstream roadmap
+item or authorize publication. The owner's local-only rule supersedes upstream
+push and pull-request instructions. Referenced sibling `craftrules` is not
+available in the approved source snapshot.
+
+The private `dobe-inspect` executable uses the existing native, WebAssembly and
+JavaScript analyzers. It reads one explicitly authorized regular input, checks
+its expected SHA-256 and writes one new structured evidence artifact. It never
+executes input code, follows dependencies, extracts archives, contacts services,
+opens an editor, or starts the upstream agent loop. The runtime must separately
+enforce tenant and permitted-file policy; a private command-line assertion is
+not a substitute for that authorization boundary.
+
+The supported profile is `static-artifact-v1`. Native inputs are ELF, PE and
+Mach-O files; WebAssembly and JavaScript use explicit format selection. Input is
+bounded to 16 MiB, JavaScript to 2 MiB and output to 32 MiB. Static observations
+do not establish execution behavior, safety, ownership or a complete dependency
+graph. Parser warnings, fallback modes and truncation remain visible. Reports
+contain untrusted target data and must never be interpreted as instructions.
+
+The analysis module owns evidence construction; the CLI is a bounded file
+transport. Existing upstream tools and defaults are unchanged. Output includes
+the pinned source revision, input hash, analyzer parameters and canonical
+upstream evidence ID. Exact original bytes belong in the runtime's portable
+project. Public admission, durable jobs, replay, recovery, packaging and Linux
+qualification remain required before release.
